  "notes": "Lighthouse keeper: a cozy seaside kit. 32x32 keeper (idle, 6-frame walks, a lantern raise that plays once), 16px beach and lighthouse-interior tiles, larger props (lighthouse 24x48, stair 32x32, table 32x24, rug 44x26). The keeper walks right by mirroring left. The art's room maps (rooms/*.map) are not part of the pack. Agent-made pixel art (pxart .px sources in pxart/). Animated tiles: variant_group = animation, frames <file>/<group>/<n>.png in play order (frames@ms): shore 2@600ms, water 2@500ms. A kit's ground_tiles already animates the ones its grid chars use. Each character_frame's fps (in the loaded manifest) is the art's own timing; Sprites.animate() uses it unless you pass {fps}. Palette variant (recolour of the whole pack, unrelated to tile variant groups) `night`: the art's own palette (colours a variant doesn't set, like lights, keep their base colour); the colours and descriptions above are the base palette's. `night`: cool moonlight over beach, keeper and interior; the lamp colours stay lit. Prefix any path, character, variant_group or kit name with `night/`, e.g. Sprites.animate('night/keeper', 'idle', null), Sprites.object('night/world/crate.png'), Sprites.kit('night/beach'); a `night/` kit's ground_tiles and ground_colors are night too, and Sprites.fitCanvas(canvas, {kit: 'night/beach'}) frames the canvas in it. Light a scene with one palette: don't mix `night/` art with base art in the same view. Not in schema v1, not exported: per-frame durations (keeper lantern/down \u2014 no fps emitted); play-count (keeper lantern/down x1)."
 },
